  "result": "Perfect! All 93 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Summary of additions:**\n\n1. **src/numbering.js** \u2014 New module with one function:\n   - `nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` \u2014 Generates the next invoice number in format `INV-<year>-<4-digit-counter>`. Counters restart each year. Handles unordered input and ignores malformed numbers.\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 One new function:\n   - `issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)` \u2014 Issues a draft invoice by assigning it a number and changing status to 'issued'. Returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` if the invoice isn't a draft. Doesn't mutate the original invoice.\n\n3. **test/numbering.test.js** \u2014 12 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Empty arrays and counter initialization\n   - Counter incrementing and year-based separation\n   - Unordered arrays and malformed numbers\n   - Large counter values and zero-padding\n   - Year boundaries and multiple years\n   - Duplicate handling\n\n4. **test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 9 new issueInvoice tests covering:\n   - Happy path with empty and existing numbers\n   - Property preservation\n   - Status validation (NOT_DRAFT errors)\n   - Non-mutation of original invoices\n   - Multiple invoices with unique numbers\n   - Year-boundary behavior\n   - Integration with addLine\n\nAll calculations use correct integer cents format and follow the house rules.",
